This project demonstrates the design and implementation of a secure, scalable hybrid network architecture connecting an on-premises data center to AWS.
The architecture follows AWS best practices for security, high availability, and network segmentation using Transit Gateway, Site-to-Site VPN, and private VPC design.
The goal is to enable secure private connectivity, centralized traffic control, and future scalability for multi-VPC environments.

🎯 Objectives

Securely connect on-premises infrastructure to AWS

Centralize routing and control using AWS Transit Gateway

Implement defense-in-depth network security

Enable high availability and failover

Provide visibility and monitoring for network traffic
